# Cursor Rules for ChekiLens

You are developing ChekiLens, an iOS 18 native Polaroid/Cheki scanning and idol fan archival app.

## Mandatory Step Before Any Code Generation:
1. Always read `docs/PROGRESS.md` first to know the exact atomic task.
2. Check `git status` to see the current working directory state.
3. Only implement ONE atomic task per turn.
4. When done, update `docs/PROGRESS.md` with `[x]` and update the Next Action summary.

## Code Standards:
- Swift 6 & iOS 17/18 SwiftUI.
- Apple Human Interface Guidelines: strictly follow mockups in `docs/ui/`.
- SwiftData for all persistent models (`@Model`).
- Apple Vision framework (`VNDetectRectanglesRequest`, `VNRecognizeTextRequest`).
- Core Image (`CIPerspectiveCorrection`).
- Avoid third-party dependencies unless strictly necessary.

## UI Work (Mandatory):
- Before touching anything under `ChekiLens/Sources/Views/` (UI, UX, animation, gesture), read `docs/UI_AGENT_GUIDELINES.md` and follow it. It overrides existing per-screen code.
- Use shared chrome components only (44 pt circle/capsule), `xmark` / `checkmark` for toolbar cancel/confirm, yellow for active camera states, `ChekiMotion` for animations, and "live-follow pinch, commit on release" for grid zoom.
- After a UI task, update §9 of `docs/UI_AGENT_GUIDELINES.md` as well as `docs/PROGRESS.md`.
